  "adaptations": [
    "Canonical public terminal contracts; Host/Client types share SDK identity",
    "Application recording uses an injected port; native/file implementations stay in adapters",
    "Admission revocation, metadata-only observations and accurate closing-resource task facts",
    "Local file behavior moves from the former shell HTTP capability server to an owned Host adapter, live grant leases and pinned fs-safe primitives; no Electron or HTTP business dispatch is copied.",
    "Transfers separates immutable IO reservations, selected file/connection leases, native tar staging, durable facts and coalesced realtime progress; browser projections adapt the already owned Files observation pattern.",
    "Serial/Telnet reuse frozen protocol adapters behind Connections-owned opens and Terminals-owned sessions; actual native close barriers, bounded negotiation, canceled-create draining and conservative failed-handle ownership strengthen teardown.",
    "SSH tunnels split profile facts/application policy from native forwarding; opaque Catalog/Connections transaction participants validate Host references, while unique address dispatch, half-close-aware piping, bounded SOCKS/control resources and actual teardown barriers preserve ownership.",
    "RemoteDesktop joins existing RDP/VNC/SPICE session metadata, transient claims and binary protocol semantics behind selected Connections stream leases. Strict generation and resource admission, pending creation/channel reservations, actual native close barriers, bounded queues, explicit public DTO identity and metadata-only Client projection strengthen teardown without changing upstream clients or vendor code.",
    "Automation retains existing command hierarchy, trigger matching/control notation and batch policy behind owned SQL and selected Catalog/Terminals/Connections ports. Owned revisions and compact receipts replace app_meta access; durable commit precedes worker activation/cancellation, Profile/generation leases survive until actual native close, and the existing Axterm Catalog fragment pattern supplies atomic Client facts. Live trigger state refreshes only after commit and fails closed on invalid storage.",
    "Reviewed file rename retains frozen template/date/filter behavior behind a selected grant-scoped native port. Exclusive native no-replace moves, preview identity checks, bounded generation receipts, complete transient Client baselines, cancellation-aware rollback and same-directory reauthorization for uncertain recovery replace retained raw paths and swallowed rollback failures. Reconnect never replays filesystem mutations.",
    "Workspace ports the frozen Axterm chrome ownership, class names and computed style inputs into a real root/typed child Slot composition. Terminal UI consumes only its Client model and bounded binary stream, owns xterm/fit/parser-completion flow and cleanup, and retains bounded paste assessment, review, cancellation and normalization. Raw clipboard text stays in transient renderer refs. Current port is a functional default-entry/PTY checkpoint, not full page or visual parity. CSS Modules compile through pinned Vite to explicit owned style effects, with a single independently loadable factory and no side-effect stylesheet injection.",
    "Configuration retains the version-one sync protocols, crypto and category precedence through owned storage, shared per-resource physical IO leases, durable one-shot intents and complete metadata models. Vault references are never deleted by sync profile CRUD; uncertain writes suspend future automatic uploads. Configuration facts, sync facts, receipts and outbox finalize atomically before preview release. All provider responses and late operations drain before teardown."
  ]
}
